2026-11-14T20:41:41.714Z [WARN] Compact cache sharing: no text in response, falling back. Response: {"message":{"type":"message","model":"GLM-5.3","usage":{"input_tokens":96327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"6878b01b97e045aea9608b3f4286eb4e","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user has asked me to summarize the conversation so far, but the actual task I was doing is the Clairvoyant intent i040 investigation. The final message says \"FINALIZE THIS INTENT NOW\" but also says respond with TEXT ONLY and no tools — the actual request in the last message is to produce a summary of the conversation (this appears to be a context-compaction request).\n\nWait — the last user message has two parts: (1) \"FINALIZE THIS INTENT NOW...\" instructions, and (2) a request to create a detailed summary of the conversation with CRITICAL instructions to respond with text only, no tools.\n\nThis is a compaction/summary request. I should produce the <analysis> and <summary> blocks capturing everything needed to continue the finalization work. The next agent (after compaction) will need to write the final artifact JSON to the findings path and call mcp__clairvoyant__done.\n\nLet me capture all the details:\n\n**Task**: Intent i040, SNAPSHOT=s10, BRANCH=unclamped-wire-count. Search only snapshots/s10 for unclamped wire counts stored into persistent kernel objects at deserialization entry points, with priority on asymmetric validation (sibling path enforces MAX, mirror path does not). Record seed usbip as excluded-by-rule if present. Write final artifact to /mnt/raid/home/.../agent-state/findings/i040.json, checkpoint at /mnt/raid/home/.../agent-state/checkpoints/i040.json, then call mcp__clairvoyant__done exactly once.\n\n**What was done so far in this session**:\n\n1. Checked TMPDIR: /mnt/raid/home/yangshuangning/vuln_variant_search/experiments/clairvoyant_variant_search/runs/10_cluster/C9/agent-state/tmp/proj_001-i040-explore. Snapshots s01..s13 exist.\n\n2. Wrote initial checkpoint to /mnt/raid/.../agent-state/checkpoints/i040.json via python3 heredoc with atomic os.replace. Content: intent_id i040, branch unclamped-wire-count, snapshot s10, status initial_checkpoint_before_search, plan with 5 steps, empty candidates and findings lists.\n\n3. Listed s10 root: it's a Linux source tree (Documentation, arch, block, certs, crypto, drivers, fs, include, init, io_uring, ipc, kernel, lib, mm, net, rust, samples, scripts, security, sound, tools, usr, virt). No Makefile at root. rg: the PATH-pinned rg at ~/.codex/... is Permission denied; /usr/bin/rg works (ripgrep 15.1.0).\n\n4. Checked seed usbip state in s10: drivers/usb/usbip/usbip_common.c lines 482-485 contain the upstream FIX:\n```c\nif (rpdu->number_of_packets < 0 ||\n    rpdu->number_of_packets > urb->number_of_packets)\n    rpdu->number_of_packets = 0;\nurb->number_of_packets = rpdu->number_of_packets;\n```\nAnd usbip_recv_iso (starting line ~675) contains the fix: `if (np <= 0 || np > USBIP_MAX_ISO_PACKETS)` at line 685-686, zeroes urb->number_of_packets = 0 at 693, uses kcalloc(np, sizeof(*iso)) at ~697. So the seed family is PATCHED in s10 → classified safe/excluded (patched), not even excluded-by-rule-unpatched; record as safe.\n\n5. Checked hci_store_wake_reason in s10 net/bluetooth/hci_event.c: at line 7576, the function in s10 has a DIFFERENT (newer) signature: `static void hci_store_wake_reason(struct hci_dev *hdev, const bdaddr_t *bdaddr, u8 addr_type)` — the caller passes bdaddr/addr_type directly; the vulnerable variant (which parsed `u8 num_reports = *ptr;` from the wire) is NOT present in s10. Call sites at 3118, 3283, 5030, 5733, 6026, 6425, 6515, 6562, 6868, 7851 all pass already-parsed bdaddr. So the previously reported finding family (f006/f015/f026/f034) is not applicable in s10 — the newer signature takes bdaddr directly. Also hci_ev_table with min_len/max_len exists (HCI_EV_VL macros etc.), meaning this tree has the modern event validation framework. Need to verify the LE adv report handlers (hci_le_adv_report_evt etc.) use hci_le_ev_skb_pull — not yet verified in this session.\n\n6. Checked drivers/md/raid5-ppl.c entries_count: present at lines 976 and 1151 with `for (i = 0; i < le32_to_cpu(pplhdr->entries_count); i++)` — the SAME unclamped on-disk count consumption reported for s07 (f017/f030) and s09 (f034). Write path enforces cap at line 281 (`io->entries_count == PPL_HDR_MAX_ENTRIES`), ppl_submit_iounit loops at 444, stores at 456. This is a candidate for reporting in s10 (unclamped on-disk count, asymmetric validation: write path enforces the cap, read/recovery path does not).\n\n7. Checked drivers/accel/qaic/qaic_control.c in s10: \n   - line 979: `user_msg->count = le32_to_cpu(msg->hdr.count);` — the decode_message store (error-unwind-poisoned-count branch material, not primarily this branch)\n   - line 1260: request-direction clamp `user_msg->count > QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH / sizeof(struct qaic_manage_trans_hdr)`\n   - lines 1449-1462: resp_worker orphan-response path with `u32 msg_count = le32_to_cpu(msg->hdr.count); u32 msg_len = le32_to_cpu(msg->hdr.len);` and the loop `for (j = 0; j < msg_count && len < msg_len; ++j)` advancing only by peer `trans_hdr->len` — the SAME resp_worker orphan loop reported for s01 (f012). This IS on-branch: unclamped wire count (hdr.count) consumed with no clamp on the orphan/mirror path while the request path (qaic_manage 1259-1261) enforces QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH — asymmetric validation. The response buffer: msg_xfer allocates `out_buf = kmalloc(QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH, GFP_KERNEL)` at line 1063 and queues it via mhi_queue_buf with QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH length — so the orphan-response buffer is a fixed QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH (4K?) buffer, and resp_worker's loop reads msg->data + len where len advances only by peer-supplied trans_hdr->len with no per-iteration bound check against the actual received length (mhi_result->bytes_xferd). The loop condition `len < msg_len` uses peer hdr.len. So if device sends count=1 with hdr.len large... actually len starts at 0, and condition is len < msg_len; first iteration reads trans_hdr at msg->data + 0 (in bounds), reads trans_hdr->type and trans_hdr->len (4-byte reads); decode_deactivate(qdev, trans_hdr, &len, NULL) is called for DEACTIVATE type; else len += trans_hdr->len. If trans_hdr->len is huge (peer-controlled), len jumps past the 4K buffer, then the next iteration reads trans_hdr at msg->data + len → OOB read (wild read at attacker-chosen offset). Also if trans_hdr->len == 0 with msg_count > 1, infinite loop. This matches the s01 f012 finding family.\n\n   I also read qaic_mhi_dl_xfer_cb (lines 1495-1516): validates only transaction_status and magic_number, then queues resp_worker — no length validation. And msg_xfer (1040-1110): out_buf = kmalloc(QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH) queued for DMA_FROM_DEVICE — the actual received length (mhi_result->bytes_xferd) is never compared to hdr.len/hdr.count anywhere in this path (based on what was read; the bytes_xferd check was flagged unresolved in prior snapshots' audits — in this session I located QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH references at 845/867/944/975/1061/1063/1070/1259-1260/1303/1323 but did not find a bytes_xferd check; rg output for bytes_xferd showed no hits, confirming no cross-check of actual received length).\n\n   Actually the rg output \"bytes_xferd\" produced no matches in qaic_control.c (the output showed only QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH lines). This strengthens: no cross-check of mhi_result->bytes_xferd against hdr.len exists in s10's qaic_control.c.\n\n**Where I was when interrupted**: I had just read msg_xfer's MHI receive path (lines 1040-1110) confirming the response buffer is kmalloc(QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH) and that the orphan path is resp_worker. The next step was to pick the strongest candidate(s) and write the final artifact. \n\nGiven the finalize directive: I must now use evidence already collected. Strongest candidates for i040 (unclamped-wire-count) in s10:\n\nCandidate 1 (REPORT): drivers/accel/qaic/qaic_control.c:1449-1462 resp_worker orphan-response loop — device-supplied hdr.count/hdr.len with no clamp (request path enforces at 1259-1261), loop advances only by peer trans_hdr->len, no cross-check against QAIC_MANAGE_MAX_MSG_LENGTH or mhi_result->bytes_xferd. Confidence: medium (matches f012 which was low-medium for s01; the mechanism is source-verified). Quote available verbatim:\n```c\n\t\tu32 msg_count = le32_to_cpu(msg->hdr.count);\n\t\tu32 msg_len = le32_to_cpu(msg->hdr.len);\n\t\tu32 len = 0;\n\t\tint j;\n\n\t\tfor (j = 0; j < msg_count && len < msg_len; ++j) {\n\t\t\tstruct wire_trans_hdr *trans_hdr;\n\n\t\t\ttrans_hdr = (struct wire_trans_hdr *)(msg->data + len);\n```\nLines 1449-1455. Report range could be 1449-1462.\n\nCandidate 2 (REPORT or candidate-reported): drivers/md/raid5-ppl.c:976-998 ppl_recover() and 1151 ppl_load_distributed() — on-disk entries_count unclamped against PPL_HDR_MAX_ENTRIES; write path enforces at 281. Same instance family as f017 (s07) and f030/f034 (s09). For the unclamped-wire-count branch this fits (on-disk count crossing trust boundary, no range check, asymmetric validation). Prior snapshots reported this on both unclamped-wire-count (f030, s07; f034, s09) and error-unwind branches.\n\nCandidate 3 (safe/excluded): usbip seed family in s10 is PATCHED (clamp at 482-485, recv_iso validation+reset at 685-693, kcalloc) — record as safe, excluded from findings per seed rule.\n\nCandidate 4 (safe): net/bluetooth/hci_event.c hci_store_wake_reason in s10 has the newer signature taking (hdev, bdaddr, addr_type) — no num_reports wire parse; the vulnerable variant is absent. Also should note LE adv handlers presumably use hci_le_ev_skb_pull (modern table with min_len/max_len exists) but not verified — could be listed as safe with caveat or leave as limitation.\n\nCandidates not yet verified in s10 (limitations): ceph_fill_fragtree nsplits, dlm member num_slots, cifs parse_dfs_referrals NumberOfReferrals, qaic decode_message count store (error-unwind branch), broad sweep of netlink/ioctl count stores — not performed before finalize directive.\n\nThe finalize directive allows at most four targeted Read/Bash calls to obtain exact source lines. I already have exact lines for qaic resp_worker (1449-1462 read verbatim) and raid5-ppl (976, 1151 line numbers from rg, with content `for (i = 0; i < le32_to_cpu(pplhdr->entries_count); i++) {` — line 976 exact content known; for the quote I might want lines 976-980 exact text. I have from the rg output: line 976 `for (i = 0; i < le32_to_cpu(pplhdr->entries_count); i++) {` and line 1151 `for (i = 0; i < le32_to_cpu(pplhdr->entries_count); i++)`. The s07/s09 facts contain the fuller snippet: `struct ppl_header_entry *e = &pplhdr->entries[i]; u32 pp_size = le32_to_cpu(e->pp_size);`. For the final artifact, I should use a quote that occurs literally in the reported range. Safest: quote the single line 976 content for raid5-ppl, and for qaic quote the lines I read verbatim (1449-1455).\n\nFinal artifact structure (schema v1):\n- version: 1\n- intent_id: \"i040\"\n- branch: \"unclamped-wire-count\"\n- execution_status: \"complete\"\n- snapshots_checked: [\"s10\"]\n- findings: 1-2 findings (qaic resp_worker as primary; raid5-ppl as second)\n- candidates: list with statuses (qaic resp_worker reported; raid5-ppl reported; usbip safe/patched; hci_store_wake_reason safe-absent; possibly qaic decode_message noted; ceph/dlm/cifs unexamined → maybe put in limitations only, or as unresolved candidates — the schema allows candidates with status unresolved)\n- limitations: bounded sweep halted by finalize directive; broad netlink/ioctl count-store sweep not performed; ceph nsplits/dlm num_slots/cifs NumberOfReferrals not verified in s10; imp